[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   Step 131: Bipolar cone-shell coherence (step_b95).
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   Follow-on to step_129's bipolar unification test.  If the two eras'
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   transit structures are segments of one shell-like boundary at fixed
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   angular radius about the CMB-anchored bipolar axis, the slip residual
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   should organize by bipolar cone angle and peak on a ring at a shared
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   cone radius rather than at the axis pole.
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   Runs entirely on the independent two-leg refit checkpoints (step_b91,
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   step_b92); the CMB bipolar axis is the externally declared frame axis
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   (step_125 convention).  Look-elsewhere is priced inside every
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   permutation null by re-maximizing the same cell grid / ring scan on
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   each draw.
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   T1  Per-era cone x side profile (15-deg cone bands x apex/antapex)
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   of the kick-regressed log-rotation residual.  Extremeness of the
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   modal cell under a max-statistic permutation null.
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   T2  Common-cone joint test on the two measured anomaly axes: the
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   declared axis (48.5 deg, antapex side) and the displaced axis
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   (53.8 deg, apex side) lie in the same 45-60 deg cone band on
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   opposite sides of the bipolar axis.  Null: independent isotropic
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   direction pairs; reports the joint probability of the observed
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   band-membership-plus-opposite-side configuration.  The resident
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   detached axis (64.1 deg) is reported alongside honestly.
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   T3  Ring-versus-pole morphology: per era a Gaussian ring profile
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   centred at cone angle theta0 is scanned over theta0 and the best
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   ring amplitude compared against the pole (theta0 = 0) contrast;
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   a shell peaks away from the pole.  Permutation null re-scans.
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   T4  Band-resident amplitude contrast: per era, residual inside the
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   union band (45-60 deg, era-correct side) versus the rest of the
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   sphere -- Mann-Whitney and permutation p, plus the cross-era
[2026-09-21 15:16:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 131]   product extremeness.
